IMPORT prelude

-- International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009 (Singapore) -- the Cape Town Convention and Aircraft Protocol as given the
-- force of law by s 3: which aircraft objects are covered (Protocol Art I(2)(b), (e), (l)), when the Convention applies (Convention
-- Arts 3, 4; Protocol Art IV(1)), how an international interest is constituted (Convention Arts 7, 11; Protocol Art VII), priority
-- (Convention Arts 29(1), (2), 30(1), 39(3); Protocol Art XIV(1), (2)), the creditor's notice and de-registration remedies
-- (Protocol Art IX(2), (4)), and the Act's own insolvency remedy (ss 2(1) "commencement of insolvency proceedings", 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IIAEA2009.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the body is 40/2019 (s 5). The deposit's metadata calls it the current version as at 01 Oct 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0104 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The people it decides things for are airlines, lessors, financiers, buyers of aircraft and engines, and the
-- liquidators and judicial managers of an insolvent operator. SCOPED to those decisions. Not encoded: the International Registry's
-- machinery (Convention Chapters IV to VII), assignments (Chapter IX), relief pending final determination (Art 13, Protocol Art X),
-- jurisdiction (Chapter XII and s 5), the vesting and redemption rules (Art 9), the surplus distribution (Art 8(5), (6)), the
-- treaty's final clauses, and the Third Schedule consolidated text (an interpretive aid only, s 3(3)). SINGAPORE'S DECLARATIONS ARE
-- NOT IN THE DEPOSIT: s 3(1)(b) applies the treaty "to Singapore as described in the declarations", so whatever the declarations
-- add or withhold (Art 39 categories, Art 54 remedies, Art XXX) is not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earlier of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `Protocol Art I(2)(b), (e), (l) -- which equipment is an aircraft object`

-- Art I(2)(b): "aircraft engines" -- other than those used in "military, customs or police services" -- powered by jet propulsion
-- or turbine or piston technology and "(i) in the case of jet propulsion aircraft engines, have at least 1750 lb of thrust or its
-- equivalent; and (ii) in the case of turbine-powered or piston-powered aircraft engines, have at least 550 rated take-off shaft
-- horsepower or its equivalent".
DECLARE EngineKind IS ONE OF
    `a jet engine`
    `a turbine or piston engine`

GIVEN `the engine kind` IS AN EngineKind, `thrust in lb` IS A NUMBER, `rated take-off shaft horsepower` IS A NUMBER,
      `used in military, customs or police services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the engine is an aircraft engine` IF
        NOT `used in military, customs or police services`
    AND CONSIDER `the engine kind`
        WHEN `a jet engine` THEN `thrust in lb` AT LEAST 1750
        WHEN `a turbine or piston engine` THEN `rated take-off shaft horsepower` AT LEAST 550

-- Art I(2)(e): "airframes" type certified to transport "(i) at least eight (8) persons including crew; or (ii) goods in excess of
-- 2750 kilograms". Art I(2)(l): "helicopters" type certified to transport "(i) at least five (5) persons including crew; or
-- (ii) goods in excess of 450 kilograms". Both exclude military, customs or police use. "At least" persons, but goods "in excess of".
DECLARE AirframeKind IS ONE OF
    `an airframe`
    `a helicopter`

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN AirframeKind, `persons certified including crew` IS A NUMBER, `goods certified in kg` IS A NUMBER,
      `used in military, customs or police services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the airframe or helicopter is an aircraft object` IF
        NOT `used in military, customs or police services`
    AND CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `an airframe` THEN `persons certified including crew` AT LEAST 8 OR `goods certified in kg` GREATER THAN 2750
        WHEN `a helicopter` THEN `persons certified including crew` AT LEAST 5 OR `goods certified in kg` GREATER THAN 450

§§ `Convention Arts 3, 4 and Protocol Art IV(1) -- when the Convention applies`

-- Art 3(1): the Convention applies when, "at the time of the conclusion of the agreement", the debtor is situated in a Contracting
-- State; (2) the creditor's location does not matter. Art 4(1): situated where (a) incorporated or formed, (b) registered office or
-- statutory seat, (c) centre of administration, or (d) place of business -- (2) the principal place if more than one, or the
-- habitual residence if none.
-- Protocol Art IV(1): it ALSO applies to a helicopter, or an airframe pertaining to an aircraft, "registered in an aircraft register
-- of a Contracting State which is the State of registry".
GIVEN `incorporated or formed in a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN, `registered office in a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `centre of administration in a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN, `principal place of business or habitual residence in a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the airframe or helicopter is on a Contracting State's aircraft register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Convention applies` IF
        `incorporated or formed in a Contracting State`
    OR  `registered office in a Contracting State`
    OR  `centre of administration in a Contracting State`
    OR  `principal place of business or habitual residence in a Contracting State`
    OR  `the airframe or helicopter is on a Contracting State's aircraft register`

§§ `Convention Art 7 and Protocol Art VII -- constituting an international interest`

-- Art 7: an interest is constituted as an international interest where the agreement "(a) is in writing; (b) relates to an object of
-- which the chargor, conditional seller or lessor has power to dispose; (c) enables the object to be identified in conformity with
-- the Protocol; and (d) in the case of a security agreement, enables the secured obligations to be determined, but without the need
-- to state a sum or maximum sum secured".
-- Protocol Art VII: a description containing "its manufacturer's serial number, the name of the manufacturer and its model
-- designation is necessary and sufficient" to identify the object.
DECLARE AgreementKind IS ONE OF
    `a security agreement`
    `a title reservation agreement`
    `a leasing agreement`

GIVEN `serial number stated` IS A BOOLEAN, `manufacturer named` IS A BOOLEAN, `model designation stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the object is identified` IF
    `serial number stated` AND `manufacturer named` AND `model designation stated`

GIVEN `the agreement kind` IS AN AgreementKind, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `has power to dispose` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `serial number stated` IS A BOOLEAN, `manufacturer named` IS A BOOLEAN, `model designation stated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `secured obligations determinable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an international interest is constituted` IF
        `in writing`
    AND `has power to dispose`
    AND `the object is identified` `serial number stated` `manufacturer named` `model designation stated`
    AND CONSIDER `the agreement kind`
        WHEN `a security agreement` THEN `secured obligations determinable`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Art 11: the parties "may at any time agree in writing as to the events that constitute a default"; (2) where they have not, default
-- "means a default which substantially deprives the creditor of what it is entitled to expect under the agreement".
GIVEN `default events agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `an agreed event has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the creditor is substantially deprived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a default` IF
    IF `default events agreed in writing` THEN `an agreed event has occurred` ELSE `the creditor is substantially deprived`

§§ `Convention Arts 29, 30(1), 39(3) and Protocol Art XIV -- priority`

-- Art 29(1): "A registered interest has priority over any other interest subsequently registered and over an unregistered interest."
-- (2) "even if the first-mentioned interest was acquired or registered with actual knowledge of the other interest". Registration
-- times are entered as numbers on one scale; the earlier number was registered first.
GIVEN `first is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `first registered at` IS A NUMBER, `second is registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `second registered at` IS A NUMBER, `the first holder knew of the second interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first interest has priority over the second` IF
    `first is registered` AND ((NOT `second is registered`) OR `first registered at` LESS THAN `second registered at`)

-- Protocol Art XIV (replacing Convention Art 29(3) for aircraft, by Art III): (1) a buyer "under a registered sale" acquires free from
-- an interest subsequently registered and from an unregistered interest, "even if the buyer has actual knowledge"; (2) a buyer
-- acquires "subject to an interest registered at the time of its acquisition". (2) does not require the sale to be registered.
-- An interest registered after the acquisition but before the sale is registered fits neither paragraph; this encoding returns
-- `left to the applicable law` for it (an inference: the Protocol does not settle it, and Convention Art 5(2) sends unsettled
-- questions to general principles or the applicable law).
DECLARE BuyerPosition IS ONE OF
    `takes subject to the interest`
    `takes free of the interest`
    `left to the applicable law`

GIVEN `interest is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `interest registered at` IS A NUMBER, `buyer acquired at` IS A NUMBER,
      `sale is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `sale registered at` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BuyerPosition
`the buyer's position` MEANS
    IF `interest is registered` AND `interest registered at` AT MOST `buyer acquired at`
    THEN `takes subject to the interest`
    ELSE IF `sale is registered` AND ((NOT `interest is registered`) OR `interest registered at` GREATER THAN `sale registered at`)
         THEN `takes free of the interest`
         ELSE `left to the applicable law`

-- Protocol Art XIV(3): "Ownership of or another right or interest in an aircraft engine shall not be affected by its installation on or
-- removal from an aircraft." Not given a rule: it has no inputs that change the answer. Recorded in NOTES.md.

-- Art 30(1): "In insolvency proceedings against the debtor an international interest is effective if PRIOR to the commencement of the
-- insolvency proceedings that interest was registered". (2) it may still be effective under the applicable law -- not modelled.
GIVEN `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `registered at` IS A NUMBER, `insolvency commenced at` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is effective in the insolvency under Article 30` IF
    `is registered` AND `registered at` LESS THAN `insolvency commenced at`

-- Art 39(3): "A non-consensual right or interest has priority over an international interest if and only if the former is of a
-- category covered by a declaration deposited prior to the registration of the international interest." s 4(15) repeats the rule
-- for insolvency proceedings. Art 39(4) (retroactive declarations at ratification) is not modelled.
GIVEN `category covered by a declaration` IS A BOOLEAN, `declaration deposited at` IS A NUMBER, `international interest registered at` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-consensual right has priority` IF
    `category covered by a declaration` AND `declaration deposited at` LESS THAN `international interest registered at`

§§ `Protocol Art IX(2), (4) -- the creditor's remedies`

-- Art IX(1): the creditor may, "to the extent that the debtor has at any time so agreed", procure de-registration and export of the
-- aircraft. (2) "The creditor shall not exercise the remedies ... without the prior consent in writing of the holder of any
-- registered interest ranking in priority to that of the creditor." By Art IV(3) the parties cannot vary Art IX(2) to (4).
GIVEN `the debtor agreed to the remedy` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is a default` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a higher-ranking registered interest exists` IS A BOOLEAN, `its holder consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor may procure de-registration and export` IF
        `the debtor agreed to the remedy`
    AND `there is a default`
    AND ((NOT `a higher-ranking registered interest exists`) OR `its holder consented in writing`)

-- Art IX(4): "A chargee giving ten or more working days' prior written notice of a proposed sale or lease to interested persons
-- shall be deemed to satisfy the requirement of providing 'reasonable prior notice'". Shorter notice is not deemed unreasonable; it
-- is simply not deemed reasonable -- this rule answers only whether the safe harbour is met.
GIVEN `notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `working days of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is deemed reasonable` IF
    `notice in writing` AND `working days of notice` AT LEAST 10

§§ `s 2(1) -- when insolvency proceedings commence`

-- "commencement of insolvency proceedings" means (a) bankruptcy (IRDA Part 16): the date of presentation of the bankruptcy
-- application; (b) winding up (Part 8): the time the winding up is deemed to have commenced under s 126 or specified under s 161(6);
-- (c) voluntary arrangement (Part 14): the date of the application for an interim order; (d) compromise under Companies Act s 210:
-- the date of the application; (e) compromise under IRDA s 71: the date of the application; (f) judicial management (Part 7): the
-- date of the application for a judicial management order OR the date of lodgment of the notice of appointment of the interim
-- judicial manager.
DECLARE ProceedingKind IS ONE OF
    `bankruptcy`
    `winding up`
    `a voluntary arrangement`
    `a Companies Act section 210 compromise`
    `an IRDA section 71 compromise`
    `judicial management by court application`
    `judicial management by appointment of an interim judicial manager`

DECLARE CommencementEvent IS ONE OF
    `presentation of the bankruptcy application`
    `the deemed commencement of the winding up`
    `the application for an interim order`
    `the application to court for the compromise`
    `the application for a judicial management order`
    `lodgment of the notice of appointment of the interim judicial manager`

GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A ProceedingKind
GIVETH A CommencementEvent
`the commencement event` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proceeding`
    WHEN `bankruptcy` THEN `presentation of the bankruptcy application`
    WHEN `winding up` THEN `the deemed commencement of the winding up`
    WHEN `a voluntary arrangement` THEN `the application for an interim order`
    WHEN `a Companies Act section 210 compromise` THEN `the application to court for the compromise`
    WHEN `an IRDA section 71 compromise` THEN `the application to court for the compromise`
    WHEN `judicial management by court application` THEN `the application for a judicial management order`
    WHEN `judicial management by appointment of an interim judicial manager` THEN `lodgment of the notice of appointment of the interim judicial manager`

§§ `s 4 -- remedies on insolvency`

-- s 4(2): the section applies where (a) the debtor, "if it is a body corporate or firm, is incorporated or registered in Singapore;
-- or ... if he or she is a natural person, is domiciled in or has his or her principal place of business in Singapore"; (b) the
-- international interest has been registered; and (c) the debtor and creditor "have not by written agreement excluded" it.
DECLARE DebtorKind IS ONE OF
    `a body corporate or firm`
    `a natural person`

GIVEN `the debtor kind` IS A DebtorKind, `incorporated or registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `domiciled or principal place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the interest is registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `excluded by written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 applies` IF
        CONSIDER `the debtor kind`
        WHEN `a body corporate or firm` THEN `incorporated or registered in Singapore`
        WHEN `a natural person` THEN `domiciled or principal place of business in Singapore`
    AND `the interest is registered`
    AND NOT `excluded by written agreement`

-- s 4(14): the date is "the earlier of (a) 30 days after the commencement of insolvency proceedings; and (b) the date on which the
-- creditor would have been entitled to take possession of the aircraft object but for this section". Days are day numbers.
GIVEN `commencement day` IS A NUMBER, `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 4 deadline` MEANS
    `the earlier of` (`commencement day` PLUS 30) `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled`

-- s 4(4): the debtor or insolvency administrator "may retain possession" where, on or before the s 4(14) date, "(a) [it] has agreed to
-- perform all future obligations of the debtor under the agreement; and (b) all defaults under the agreement (other than a default
-- constituted by the commencement of the insolvency proceedings) have been cured". A day number for something that never happened
-- should be entered as a very large number.
GIVEN `commencement day` IS A NUMBER, `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled` IS A NUMBER,
      `day it agreed to perform all future obligations` IS A NUMBER, `day all other defaults were cured` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debtor side may retain the aircraft object` IF
        `day it agreed to perform all future obligations` AT MOST `the section 4 deadline` `commencement day` `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled`
    AND `day all other defaults were cured` AT MOST `the section 4 deadline` `commencement day` `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled`

-- s 4(3): where insolvency proceedings have commenced and "the aircraft object is in Singapore", the debtor (or the insolvency
-- administrator if it has custody) "must, no later than the date referred to in subsection (14), give an opportunity to the creditor
-- to take possession" -- subject to (4). Note the Act says "give an opportunity"; Protocol Art XI(2) Alternative A says "give
-- possession".
GIVEN `section 4 applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the aircraft object is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `commencement day` IS A NUMBER, `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled` IS A NUMBER,
      `day it agreed to perform all future obligations` IS A NUMBER, `day all other defaults were cured` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor must be offered possession by the deadline` IF
        `section 4 applies`
    AND `the aircraft object is in Singapore`
    AND NOT `the debtor side may retain the aircraft object` `commencement day` `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled` `day it agreed to perform all future obligations` `day all other defaults were cured`

-- s 4(13): "Subsections (3) to (8) do not apply to the insolvency administrator of the debtor if the insolvency administrator is
-- appointed on or after the date referred to in subsection (14)."
GIVEN `appointment day` IS A NUMBER, `commencement day` IS A NUMBER, `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsections 3 to 8 bind the insolvency administrator` IF
    `appointment day` LESS THAN `the section 4 deadline` `commencement day` `day the creditor would otherwise be entitled`

-- s 4(5): where the retaining party "fails to perform all future obligations ... as agreed under subsection (4)(a), the creditor may
-- IMMEDIATELY exercise the creditor's right to take possession". No second 30-day period runs.
GIVEN `retained under subsection 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to perform a future obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor may take possession immediately` IF
    `retained under subsection 4` AND `failed to perform a future obligation`

-- s 4(8): "The insolvency administrator of the debtor is to be indemnified by the creditor for all reasonable costs incurred in
-- complying with subsection (6)(a)" (preserving and maintaining the object). Only the insolvency administrator is named; a debtor
-- that preserves the object itself is not.
DECLARE Custodian IS ONE OF
    `the insolvency administrator`
    `the debtor itself`

GIVEN `the custodian` IS A Custodian, `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `incurred preserving and maintaining the object` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor must indemnify the preservation cost` IF
        `the cost is reasonable`
    AND `incurred preserving and maintaining the object`
    AND CONSIDER `the custodian`
        WHEN `the insolvency administrator` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the debtor itself` THEN FALSE

-- s 4(10): "No obligation of the debtor under the agreement may be modified under the relevant insolvency law except with the
-- creditor's consent." (11): this does not affect the insolvency administrator's right to TERMINATE the agreement.
DECLARE InsolvencyStep IS ONE OF
    `modify an obligation of the debtor`
    `terminate the agreement`

GIVEN `the step` IS AN InsolvencyStep, `the creditor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insolvency law step is not barred by section 4` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `modify an obligation of the debtor` THEN `the creditor consented`
    WHEN `terminate the agreement` THEN TRUE
